## Safety First: Layering Determinism Under AI

Adapting to non-standardized interfaces with AI buys immense coverage, but it sacrifices determinism. A standardized interface is a contract; an agent reading a portal relies on an inference that *can* be wrong. For a system tasked with physical infrastructure safety, that risk must be heavily engineered against.

The architecture addresses this risk by **layering on determinism**:

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           PROBABILISTIC AGENT LAYER (AI)               │
│  Extraction • Control UI • Interactive Analysis        │
└───────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
                            │ (Arm-Gated & Audited)
┌───────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────┐
│           DETERMINISTIC GROUNDED CORE                  │
│  Local Messaging • Physics Detectors • On-Site DB      │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

```

* **The Deterministic Core:** An always-on, safety-critical loop consisting of a local messaging fabric and an on-site database feeding physics-grounded detectors. This layer is entirely free of LLMs and never enters the physical actuation path without an explicit, armed, and audited gate.
* **The Probabilistic Agent Layer:** Handles tasks where AI uniquely excels—universal interface extraction, configuration construction, and natural-language analysis.

### The Power of Grounding

The ultimate antidote to an incorrect AI inference is physical grounding. For instance, during testing, an AI-generated coil-temperature ("heat-margin") model was automatically *rejected* because it computed a physically impossible temperature of -118°C. Fundamental conservation laws and known physical constants provide a ground truth that the inference must agree with to be executed.

Safety is thus managed via a strict **autonomy gradient**:

$$\text{Observe} \longrightarrow \text{Alert} \longrightarrow \text{Recommend} \longrightarrow \text{Act}$$

Promotion to the next level of autonomy is always deliberate, arm-gated, and logged, keeping the agent layer out of the always-on actuation path except through these secure checkpoints.

