## The Strategic Consequence: Knowledge as the Moat

If AI agents successfully commoditize integration, software adapters cease to be the valuable component of the product—anyone can point an agent at a portal.

Instead, the durable, scarce asset becomes the **operating knowledge**: the encoded runbooks, the physics groundings, the failure taxonomies, the safety gates, and the proprietary system models. Fifteen years of deep domain experience identifying what a failing valve actually looks like, and knowing exactly what is safe to do about it—**that is the moat.** The agent simply makes that knowledge instantly deployable.

